            <title xml:id="title_ffbfe838" xml:lang="en">From the Sketchbook</title>
            <title type="subordinate" xml:id="title_ceebcd32" xml:lang="da">Smaa Klaverstykker</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_5c83e591">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_id7b14b303">Niels W. Gade</persName>
               <persName role="dedicatee" xml:id="persName_eeec29ec">Mathilde Gade</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_id4f1469ff">
               <date isodate="1857" xml:id="date_0af40ca1">spring 1857</date>
               <geogName xml:id="geogName_id8252f151">Copenhagen</geogName>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_id313436ba">
               <p xml:id="idm84">Gade composed these small piano pieces from April to June 1857 as a sort of "musical love letters" to his fiancée Mathilde Stæger, foster-daughter of his friend and publisher Emil Erslev. They were not published until 1886; however, when the autographs appeared in a private collection in May 2018 it became apparent that not alle pieces were included in "From the sketchbook". The unpublished pieces are: "Til den lille Due" (NWGW 86); "En hemmelig Hilsen" (NWGW 88); "Noget om Dur og Moll" (NWGW 90); "Godmorgen til Mathilde" (NWGW 92); and "Til Mathilde" (NWGW 95). Apart from changing the titles, Gade did not revise the pieces included in "From the Sketchbook".</p>
            </history>
